1125:      * Creates a new data stream that contains the given elements. The elements should be the same
1126:      * or be the subclass to the {@code typeInfo} type. The sequence of elements must not be empty.
1127:      *
1128:      * <p>NOTE: This creates a non-parallel data stream source by default (parallelism of one).
1129:      * Adjustment of parallelism is supported via {@code setParallelism()} on the result.
1130:      *
1131:      * @param typeInfo The type information of the elements.
1132:      * @param data The array of elements to create the data stream from.
1133:      * @param <OUT> The type of the returned data stream
1134:      * @return The data stream representing the given array of elements
1135:      */
1136:     @SafeVarargs
1137:     public final <OUT> DataStreamSource<OUT> fromData(TypeInformation<OUT> typeInfo, OUT... data) {
1138:         if (data.length == 0) {
1139:             throw new IllegalArgumentException(
1140:                     "fromElements needs at least one element as argument");
1141:         }
1142:         return fromData(Arrays.asList(data), typeInfo);
1143:     }
