684:      * Sets the state backend that describes how to store operator. It defines the data structures
685:      * that hold state during execution (for example hash tables, RocksDB, or other data stores).
686:      *
687:      * <p>State managed by the state backend includes both keyed state that is accessible on {@link
688:      * org.apache.flink.streaming.api.datastream.KeyedStream keyed streams}, as well as state
689:      * maintained directly by the user code that implements {@link
690:      * org.apache.flink.streaming.api.checkpoint.CheckpointedFunction CheckpointedFunction}.
