747:     /**
748:      * Enable the change log for current state backend. This change log allows operators to persist
749:      * state changes in a very fine-grained manner. Currently, the change log only applies to keyed
750:      * state, so non-keyed operator state and channel state are persisted as usual. The 'state' here
751:      * refers to 'keyed state'. Details are as follows:
752:      *
753:      * <p>Stateful operators write the state changes to that log (logging the state), in addition to
754:      * applying them to the state tables in RocksDB or the in-mem Hashtable.
755:      *
756:      * <p>An operator can acknowledge a checkpoint as soon as the changes in the log have reached
757:      * the durable checkpoint storage.
758:      *
759:      * <p>The state tables are persisted periodically, independent of the checkpoints. We call this
760:      * the materialization of the state on the checkpoint storage.
761:      *
762:      * <p>Once the state is materialized on checkpoint storage, the state changelog can be truncated
763:      * to the corresponding point.
764:      *
765:      * <p>It establish a way to drastically reduce the checkpoint interval for streaming
766:      * applications across state backends. For more details please check the FLIP-158.
767:      *
768:      * <p>If this method is not called explicitly, it means no preference for enabling the change
769:      * log. Configs for change log enabling will override in different config levels
770:      * (job/local/cluster).
