59: /**
60:  * A config to define the behavior of the program execution. It allows to define (among other
61:  * options) the following settings:
62:  *
63:  * <ul>
64:  *   <li>The default parallelism of the program, i.e., how many parallel tasks to use for all
65:  *       functions that do not define a specific value directly.
66:  *   <li>The number of retries in the case of failed executions.
67:  *   <li>The delay between execution retries.
68:  *   <li>The {@link ExecutionMode} of the program: Batch or Pipelined. The default execution mode is
69:  *       {@link ExecutionMode#PIPELINED}
70:  *   <li>Enabling or disabling the "closure cleaner". The closure cleaner pre-processes the
71:  *       implementations of functions. In case they are (anonymous) inner classes, it removes unused
72:  *       references to the enclosing class to fix certain serialization-related problems and to
73:  *       reduce the size of the closure.
74:  *   <li>The config allows to register types and serializers to increase the efficiency of handling
75:  *       <i>generic types</i> and <i>POJOs</i>. This is usually only needed when the functions
76:  *       return not only the types declared in their signature, but also subclasses of those types.
77:  * </ul>
78:  */
